\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each fixed regular degree $d\geq 3$, does sufficiently weak fixed iid Anderson disorder on uniform random d-regular graphs yield a positive continuous bulk density and GOE local point-process limits at every energy in the stated bulk interval, after scaling by that limiting density?

